# Network-hardening preflight stop — 2026-09-22

The isolated Fail2ban configuration comparison stopped at an assertion before
any operational configuration was changed. The candidate is confined to the
protected offline copy; the live sshd jail still targets ssh/22.

Observed difference: exactly one generated multi-set command for sshd/nftables
changed. In addition to its port property, Fail2ban expands that port into the
actionstart and actionflush command templates. The comparison incorrectly
expected only the port property to change and therefore rejected the otherwise
expected expansion. This is a validation-harness limitation, not evidence of
an unexpected live firewall or jail change.

Next validation must compare all generated commands and require differences
only in sshd/nftables port, actionstart and actionflush, with exact substitution
of the service ssh by 2222. Every other field must remain byte-identical.
Then remove the isolated override and verify the original dump is restored.
Back up the isolated override before removal. No activation until this passes,
the plan and rollback are committed/pushed, and privileged execution is available.

